flow "Transactional outbox"
summary "Writes domain state and an outbox event in one database transaction so a relay can publish reliably without dual-write data loss."
tags messaging transactions reliability
level intermediate
source "https://microservices.io/patterns/data/transactional-outbox.html"
related distributed-systems/inbox-idempotency distributed-systems/saga-compensation

node client "Client" actor
node svc "Order Service" service tone=primary
group db "Orders Database"
node orders "orders table" db in=db
node outbox "outbox table" db in=db
node relay "Outbox Relay" service
node broker "Message Broker" queue
edge client > svc
edge svc > orders
edge svc > outbox
edge outbox > relay
edge relay > broker
array status "Outbox row #42" keys=order,outbox,broker = - - -

scenario publish "Atomic write and relay publish"
  step tx "Write order and outbox in one TX"
    "Updating a database and publishing to a broker separately is a **dual write** that can leave them out of sync. Instead, the service writes both `orders` and `outbox` inside one local ACID transaction."
    send client > svc "CreateOrder"
    state svc active
    send svc > orders "INSERT #42"
    send svc > outbox "INSERT OrderCreated" with
    label status#order "saved"
    label status#outbox "pending" with
    state orders,outbox success with
  step poll "Relay reads unpublished rows"
    "A separate relay process (polling or reading the DB WAL via CDC) picks up unpublished rows from `outbox`."
    detail "Message relays use either the **Polling Publisher** pattern—querying the `outbox` table periodically, which is database-agnostic but adds polling queries—or **Transaction Log Tailing**, which tails the database commit log (WAL/binlog) for low-latency streaming without extra read load on the outbox table."
    send outbox > relay "row #42 (pending)"
    state relay active
  step emit "Publish event to broker"
    "The relay publishes `OrderCreated` to the message broker. Even if the broker was briefly unreachable earlier, the row stayed safe in the database."
    send relay > broker "OrderCreated #42"
    label status#broker "published"
    state broker success with
  step mark "Mark outbox row sent"
    "Once the broker acknowledges the publish, the relay marks row `#42` as `sent` so it is not picked up again."
    send relay > outbox "UPDATE sent=true"
    label status#outbox "sent"
    state relay,status#outbox success with

scenario relay-crash "Relay crashes before marking sent" from=publish/emit
  step crash "Relay dies after broker publish"
    "The broker already accepted `OrderCreated #42`, but the relay crashes before updating `sent=true` in the outbox table."
    state relay error
    effect relay shake
    callout outbox "Still marked pending!"
  step duplicate "Restarted relay publishes a duplicate"
    "When the relay restarts, it sees row `#42` is still `pending` and publishes `OrderCreated #42` a second time. The outbox guarantees **at-least-once** delivery, so consumers must be idempotent."
    state relay warning
    send outbox > relay "row #42 (pending)"
    send relay > broker "OrderCreated #42 (dup)"
    label status#broker "published x2"
    state status#broker warning with
    callout broker "Duplicate! Consumer needs deduplication"
